---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Praneeth Paikray, a Solutions Architect working on production AI systems, agent evaluation, and technical education.">
  <header class="page-intro container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Praneeth Paikray</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="about container">
    <section class="about-panel">
      <p>Hi, I’m Praneeth. I’m a Solutions Architect focused on making ambitious AI ideas work inside real organizations.</p>
      <p>Over the last nine years, I have worked across enterprise IT, financial services, staffing, and data platforms. The recurring pattern is simple: the model is rarely the whole system. The difficult and interesting work sits around it, in data, tools, evaluation, interfaces, operations, and the judgment to know what should be automated.</p>
      <p>At Databricks, I work with teams building production GenAI and agent systems. Outside customer work, I build open-source experiments, design technical workshops, and write about what I learn.</p>
      <p>My recent work spans agent evaluation harnesses, autonomous AI engineering, document intelligence, real-time agents, and multilingual systems.</p>

      <h2>What I care about</h2>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Measured, not asserted</dt>
          <dd>A fluent demo is a starting point. Claims should survive traces, held-out tests, model swaps, and boring edge cases.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Useful technical depth</dt>
          <dd>I like explanations that preserve tradeoffs and implementation detail without turning jargon into a personality.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Reusable work</dt>
          <dd>A good workshop or demo should leave behind an asset another engineer can understand, adapt, and run.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>Find my code on <a href="https://github.com/Praneeth16">GitHub</a>, shorter updates on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/praneeth-paikray/">LinkedIn</a>, earlier essays on <a href="https://medium.com/@paikraypraneeth">Medium</a>, and models or datasets on <a href="https://huggingface.co/Praneeth">Hugging Face</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .about-panel {
    padding: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-dark);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .about-panel > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
  }

  dl div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--warm);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    dl div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
